    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by elite speed and favorable platoon matchups. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13) stands as our highest-projected asset, capitalizing on a strong matchup against Senga and maintaining high utility due to our internal weighting for stolen base potential. Joining him at the top of the board is **Trea Turner** (79.76), whose leadoff positioning and dynamic platoon edge against Poulin make him an anchor for Roto production. **Kyle Schwarber** (78.41) rounds out our elite tier; his ability to exploit the pitching profile of Poulin, combined with his projected order rank, offers a high-ceiling output for home runs and runs scored. \n\nThe optimizer prioritized **Caleb Durbin** (72.77) and **Junior Caminero** (67.69) to maximize our efficiency scores against weaker opposing arms like Sullivan and Avila. **Caleb Durbin** is a notable beneficiary of a soft matchup, where his projected plate appearances significantly boost our stolen base outlook. Conversely, **Carson Benge** (53.36) remains the most marginal start; while his leadoff spot against Edward Cabrera provides a buffer, he lacks the statistical confidence of the rest of the core. **Pedro Ramirez** (52.85) was the final man left off the starting card. Despite a respectable matchup against Senga, he fell just short of **Kazuma Okamoto** (58.45) because the model preferred the established volume and lineup security of the current starters.\n\nManagers must monitor the weather and lineup statuses closely, as several of our highest-scoring assets, including **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, **Caleb Durbin**, and **Casey Schmitt**, rely on \"Lineup Pending\" assumptions. **Yordan Alvarez** (67.78) carries a slight risk due to the presence of Bieber, an elite arm who caps his raw projection; however, his exceptional xwOBA makes him an auto-start regardless of the matchup difficulty. Ensure that **Christian Yelich** remains benched as he is confirmed ou